Enable virtio-mmio as a built-in driver (CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y) across the
QEMU Linux defconfigs so guests using memory-mapped virtio devices do not
depend on loading a module from an initramfs.

  - x86_64:          VIRTIO_MMIO was unset, add =y
  - loongarch64:     VIRTIO_MMIO was =m, switch to =y
  - arm64 (aarch64): already =y in defconfig, no change needed
  - riscv64:         already =y in defconfig, no change needed

Generated with `git diff` against the Linux source tree at ref
74fe02ce122a6103f207d29fafc8b3a53de6abaf (after 0002-enable-nvme-builtin.patch).

diff --git a/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig b/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
index ad153f82c..bd264937e 100644
--- a/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
+++ b/arch/x86/configs/x86_64_defconfig
@@ -228,6 +228,7 @@ CONFIG_DMADEVICES=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_INPUT=y
+CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y
 CONFIG_EEEPC_LAPTOP=y
 CONFIG_AMD_IOMMU=y
 CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU=y
 # CONFIG_INTEL_IOMMU_DEFAULT_ON is not set
diff --git a/arch/loongarch/configs/loongson64_defconfig b/arch/loongarch/configs/loongson64_defconfig
index 2a1c5f8b4..7e0b3d29a 100644
--- a/arch/loongarch/configs/loongson64_defconfig
+++ b/arch/loongarch/configs/loongson64_defconfig
@@ -936,7 +936,7 @@ CONFIG_UIO_PCI_GENERIC=m
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_PCI=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_BALLOON=m
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_INPUT=m
-CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=m
+CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO=y
 CONFIG_VIRTIO_MMIO_CMDLINE_DEVICES=y
 CONFIG_VHOST_NET=m
 CONFIG_VHOST_SCSI=m
